## Google login `redirect_uri` (do not send users to 127)

**Symptom:** Sign-in on `https://offerfy.cc` opens Google with `redirect_uri=http://127.0.0.1:3001/api/v1/auth/google/callback`.

**This is not `GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI` on `offerfy-api`.** Hit `:8001` directly vs the public `/api` path — they can disagree:

| Request | What it hits | Typical `redirect_uri` |
|---|---|---|
| `http://127.0.0.1:8001/v1/auth/google/start` | systemd `offerfy-api`, `.env.production` | `https://offerfy.cc/api/v1/auth/google/callback` (correct) |
| `https://offerfy.cc/api/v1/auth/google/start` | Next `:3200` rewrite → whatever was **baked** | dest `:8002` + `.env` → `http://127.0.0.1:3001/…` if the last public build used dest |

Dest `.env`: `APP_ENV=development`, `GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://127.0.0.1:3001/api/v1/auth/google/callback`. Production `.env.production`: `APP_ENV=production`, `GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://offerfy.cc/api/v1/auth/google/callback`. Do not share those three keys (`APP_ENV`, `GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI`, `AUTH_TOKEN_SECRET`).

After every public frontend build:

```bash
python3 -c "import json; print(json.load(open('/home/ruby0322/offerfy/apps/frontend/.next/routes-manifest.json'))['rewrites']['afterFiles'])"
# destination MUST be http://127.0.0.1:8001/:path*  — never :8002, never :3001
curl -sS -D - -o /dev/null --max-time 15 https://offerfy.cc/api/v1/auth/google/start | grep -i '^location:'
# redirect_uri MUST contain offerfy.cc  — never 127.0.0.1
```

Google Cloud authorized redirect URI for the public client: `https://offerfy.cc/api/v1/auth/google/callback` (dest may list `http://127.0.0.1:3001/api/v1/auth/google/callback` on the same or a second client).

